Your configured route already contains `transactionIdentifier={2}`, so it remains in the URL even when you want to query using `stan` and `rrn`.

Keep the route free of query parameters and build them entirely in code.

In `appsettings.json`:

```json
"QueryRoute": "visadirect/v1/transactionquery"
```

Replace your endpoint-building section with:

```csharp
String baseUrl = _globalSettings.VisaDirectConfigs.BaseUrl.TrimEnd('/');
String queryRoute = _globalSettings.VisaDirectConfigs.QueryRoute.TrimStart('/');

UriBuilder builder = new($"{baseUrl}/{queryRoute}");

NameValueCollection queryParams =
    HttpUtility.ParseQueryString(String.Empty);

queryParams["acquiringBIN"] =
    _globalSettings.VisaDirectConfigs.AcquiringBin;

if (!String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(transactionIdentifier))
{
    // Query using transactionIdentifier only
    queryParams["transactionIdentifier"] = transactionIdentifier.Trim();
}
else
{
    // If transactionIdentifier is absent, both STAN and RRN are required
    if (String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(stan) ||
        String.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(rrn))
    {
        throw new SGBLBadRequestException(
            "Either transactionIdentifier or both stan and rrn must be provided.");
    }

    queryParams["stan"] = stan.Trim();
    queryParams["rrn"] = rrn.Trim();
}

builder.Query = queryParams.ToString();

String endpoint = builder.Uri.ToString();
```

This produces one of these two URLs:

```text
visadirect/v1/transactionquery
    ?acquiringBIN=408999
    &transactionIdentifier=234234322342343
```

or:

```text
visadirect/v1/transactionquery
    ?acquiringBIN=408999
    &stan=123456
    &rrn=123456789012
```

Also use the exact parameter name `acquiringBIN`. Your current expression generates `acquiringBin`, which has different capitalization:

```csharp
Char.ToLowerInvariant(nameof(AcquiringBin)[0]) + nameof(AcquiringBin)[1..]
// Result: acquiringBin
```

Explicit query parameter names are clearer and safer for an external API contract.
